        "paragraphs": [
          "An observation is one independent example. A channel is a parallel measurement or grid. Normalization centers a chosen group around its average and adjusts its spread. This block compares channels and positions within each observation’s chosen channel groups.",
          "Channels declares the architecture’s channel count; it must match the connected array. Safety value is a small positive cushion used when dividing by spread. Learned scale multiplies each channel; optional learned shift adds an adjustment. The array shape stays the same.",
          "Channel groups chooses equally sized channel teams within one observation. Groups must divide channels exactly, and each team needs more than one measurement. This block uses current groups during training and evaluation, with no remembered summaries.",
